"settings.agents.more" = "Each time one connects, the window asks you first, unless you ticked “Always allow” for it — offered only for Claude Code's own `claude`, signed by Anthropic; kept 30 days at most and 7 after its last use, never with your tabs, and asked again after you press Stop; forget it here. Nothing is drawn over the page: the tab it works in wears a small dot, and Stop is on the column's foot (or the tab strip) and in File › Stop Agent (⌃⌥⌘.) until it goes. It works in tabs of its own; your tabs it can read only if you tick “Let it see my open tabs”, and never uses. It never sees passwords, card numbers, one-time codes, private tabs, cookies or Settings, and can't download or choose files. It connects through a file on this Mac only, never the network: claude mcp add search -- /path/to/Search/search-mcp.";
