"whatsnew.notes.1.0.5.new.9" = "Find says “3 of 17”, paints every match, and can match case or whole words.";
"whatsnew.notes.1.0.5.new.10" = "Downloads pause and resume.";
"whatsnew.notes.1.0.5.new.11" = "Open Link in New Tab leaves you where you are; hold ⌥ to go to it.";
"whatsnew.notes.1.0.5.new.12" = "Search can start with a fresh window: your pinned tabs, tab groups and named tabs, and none of last time's others.";
"whatsnew.notes.1.0.5.new.13" = "Intel Macs get a download of their own.";
"whatsnew.notes.1.0.5.better.0" = "Search is built for size, so all of this fits in 6.8 MB, and pages that change all the time, like a chat writing its answer, stay quick.";
"whatsnew.notes.1.0.5.better.1" = "An extension's popup window opens as a small window, as in Chrome: a password manager's vault, a sign-in.";
"whatsnew.notes.1.0.5.better.2" = "Esc closes a new tab you haven't used, and words typed into a new tab wait for you.";
"whatsnew.notes.1.0.5.better.3" = "Tampermonkey installs scripts from a link, and SingleFile saves pages again.";
"whatsnew.notes.1.0.5.better.4" = "Close Group in a tab group's menu, and one ⇧⌘T brings the whole group back.";
"whatsnew.notes.1.0.5.better.5" = "Don't Float Videos Here, in a site's card.";
"whatsnew.notes.1.0.5.better.6" = "Bringing Arc over keeps its shape: pinned pages as pinned rows, its folders as named tab groups.";
"whatsnew.notes.1.0.5.better.7" = "Too many pinned extensions no longer push the column off screen.";
"whatsnew.notes.1.0.5.better.8" = "Empty a bookmark's name and it is its icon alone on the bookmarks bar.";
"whatsnew.notes.1.0.5.fixed.0" = "A live video, on X and elsewhere, no longer jumps every few seconds.";
"whatsnew.notes.1.0.5.fixed.1" = "A site's icon follows the page: GitHub's in the dark, a chat's unread count, and each port of localhost its own.";
"whatsnew.notes.1.0.5.fixed.2" = "Pins brought over from Arc wear their icons straight away.";
"whatsnew.notes.1.0.5.fixed.3" = "The tabs come back after a video's full screen.";
"whatsnew.notes.1.0.5.fixed.4" = "A folder in the bookmarks list opens whole.";
"whatsnew.notes.1.0.5.fixed.5" = "Signing in with a passkey works on GitHub again.";
"whatsnew.notes.1.0.5.fixed.6" = "Bitwarden's passkey window, its sync and its narrow popup.";
"whatsnew.notes.1.0.5.fixed.7" = "Keys in games no longer make the Mac beep.";
"whatsnew.notes.1.0.5.fixed.8" = "History keeps localhost:3000 and localhost:4000 apart.";
"whatsnew.notes.1.0.5.fixed.9" = "Copy Image works on WhatsApp Web's photos.";
"whatsnew.notes.1.0.5.fixed.10" = "Signing in to Claude's extension finishes on claude.ai.";
"whatsnew.notes.1.0.5.fixed.11" = "The Bookmarks menu keeps its bookmarks while a tab's title keeps changing.";
"whatsnew.notes.1.0.5.fixed.12" = "Popovers keep their rounded corners on macOS 15.";
"whatsnew.notes.1.0.5.fixed.13" = "Security hardening from a third careful private report, and many smaller fixes.";
"whatsnew.notes.1.0.4.headline" = "Several windows, and a lot to discover. Most of what's new is off until you turn it on, and the card after the update offers it.";
"whatsnew.notes.1.0.4.new.0" = "Several windows. ⌘N opens one with its own tabs; drag a tab out of the row, or use Move to Window in its menu, and it moves with its page as it is. Pinned tabs are the same in every window.";
"whatsnew.notes.1.0.4.new.1" = "Tab groups, and a sidebar on the right.";
"whatsnew.notes.1.0.4.new.2" = "⌃Tab shows your recent tabs as pictures, the last one first: a quick ⌃Tab goes back to the tab you were on.";
"whatsnew.notes.1.0.4.new.3" = "Your own keyboard shortcuts, in Settings › Shortcuts.";
"whatsnew.notes.1.0.4.new.4" = "Downloads show while they happen: a small circle fills beside the other buttons, and the Finder and the Dock show the progress too. The button can stay there for good.";
"whatsnew.notes.1.0.4.new.5" = "Bring things over from Firefox, Zen, Helium, Comet, Opera, Chrome's other channels and Arc, its spaces and pinned tabs included, or from an exported file.";
"whatsnew.notes.1.0.4.new.6" = "Site shortcuts: a word of your own before a search sends it to that site, like yt cats to YouTube.";
"whatsnew.notes.1.0.4.new.7" = "Bookmarks in the order you choose, folders of your own, and a card to name a bookmark as you add it.";
"whatsnew.notes.1.0.4.new.8" = "Videos can wait for a click, and every site can start at a zoom of your choice.";
"whatsnew.notes.1.0.4.new.9" = "A double-click on a pinned tab takes it back to the page it was pinned at.";
"whatsnew.notes.1.0.4.new.10" = "Hold a back or forward swipe to pick a page from history.";
"whatsnew.notes.1.0.4.better.0" = "Scrolling asks far less of the window, and a tab still loading no longer keeps the Mac busy.";
"whatsnew.notes.1.0.4.better.1" = "Where links go, peeking at a link with a shift-click, and flicking the floating video to a corner are now on.";
"whatsnew.notes.1.0.4.better.2" = "Tab managers and other extensions see every tab, in every window.";
"whatsnew.notes.1.0.4.better.3" = "Window › Move & Resize and the Mac's tiling work with Search's window.";
"whatsnew.notes.1.0.4.better.4" = "⌘K always opens the list of your tabs, whatever the page.";
"whatsnew.notes.1.0.4.fixed.0" = "⌘← and ⌘→ go back and forward again.";
"whatsnew.notes.1.0.4.fixed.1" = "Links from Notion and other apps bring Search to the front.";
"whatsnew.notes.1.0.4.fixed.2" = "Addresses a dev server prints, like 0.0.0.0:3000, open.";
"whatsnew.notes.1.0.4.fixed.3" = "The tabs you had at quit are the ones that come back.";
"whatsnew.notes.1.0.4.fixed.4" = "The × closes a tab in the tab bar folded away with ⌘S.";
"whatsnew.notes.1.0.4.fixed.5" = "1Password, Bitwarden, NordPass, Passbolt, iCloud Passwords and the Claude extension each get their fixes.";
"whatsnew.notes.1.0.4.fixed.6" = "And many smaller fixes.";
"whatsnew.notes.1.0.3.headline" = "Security, and the mouse wheel.";
"whatsnew.notes.1.0.3.new.0" = "Copying a saved password asks for Touch ID.";
"whatsnew.notes.1.0.3.better.0" = "A mouse wheel scrolls smoothly again on x.com and pages like it.";
"whatsnew.notes.1.0.3.better.1" = "History opens at once.";
"whatsnew.notes.1.0.3.better.2" = "Music keeps playing when you switch spaces.";
"whatsnew.notes.1.0.3.better.3" = "Pop-ups need a click.";
"whatsnew.notes.1.0.3.fixed.0" = "The holes found in this week's reviews: an extension could read files outside its own folder, and a page or an ad could open another app without asking.";
"whatsnew.notes.1.0.3.fixed.1" = "Bitwarden signs in to a self-hosted server, and extension popups hear what changes while they're open.";
"whatsnew.notes.1.0.3.fixed.2" = "A link from Mail brings Search to the front, and a full-screen video no longer goes black.";
"whatsnew.notes.1.0.3.fixed.3" = "Your extensions may each ask once more for their permissions at their next update.";
"whatsnew.notes.1.0.2.headline" = "Passkeys, password managers and Google.";
"whatsnew.notes.1.0.2.new.0" = "A site's passkey button brings up the Mac's own passkey sheet: Touch ID, your iPhone, a security key.";
"whatsnew.notes.1.0.2.new.1" = "Search can be the Mac's default browser.";
"whatsnew.notes.1.0.2.new.2" = "Each off until you turn it on in Settings: a bookmarks bar, a peek at a link with a shift-click, the video that follows you to another app, pages at 120 Hz, and where a link goes.";
"whatsnew.notes.1.0.2.new.3" = "Mute a tab, share a page, copy a link as Markdown, the mouse's back and forward buttons, and spaces in the bar across the top.";
"whatsnew.notes.1.0.2.better.0" = "Faster to open, and new tabs in about 10 ms.";
"whatsnew.notes.1.0.2.better.1" = "Pages see nothing of Search that Safari doesn't show them, and a saved password is offered only on its own site.";
"whatsnew.notes.1.0.2.fixed.0" = "1Password, Bitwarden and Proton Pass.";
"whatsnew.notes.1.0.2.fixed.1" = "If passkeys still fail after the update, restart your Mac once.";
"whatsnew.notes.1.0.1.headline" = "The first update, made of a day of your replies and pull requests.";
"whatsnew.notes.1.0.1.new.0" = "Each off until you turn it on in Settings: Spaces, a sidebar that hides until the pointer reaches the edge, and the search engine of your choice.";
"whatsnew.notes.1.0.1.new.1" = "⌘S folds the sidebar away, a middle-click closes a tab, a tab can be renamed, and the Web Inspector is in the View menu.";
"whatsnew.notes.1.0.1.fixed.0" = "Search opens again on macOS 14.";
"whatsnew.notes.1.0.1.fixed.1" = "Signing in to Google no longer reloads the page over and over with iCloud Passwords installed.";
"whatsnew.notes.1.0.1.fixed.2" = "⌘1–⌘9 on every keyboard layout, Tab between a form's fields, dragging tabs, a double-click along the top to fill the screen, and the Mac's beep while typing.";
"whatsnew.notes.1.0.headline" = "The first version. A browser for the Mac with nothing in the way.";
"whatsnew.notes.1.0.new.0" = "Tabs in a row or down the side, pinned tabs that keep their place, and one field for addresses and searches.";
"whatsnew.notes.1.0.new.1" = "Ads blocked before they load; passwords and passkeys in your keychain.";
"whatsnew.notes.1.0.new.2" = "Anything on a page can be hidden; articles open in a reading mode and videos float.";
"whatsnew.notes.1.0.new.3" = "Chrome extensions from the Chrome Web Store, on macOS 15.4 or later.";
"whatsnew.notes.1.0.new.4" = "Tabs you haven't looked at for half an hour sleep and give their memory back.";
"whatsnew.notes.1.0.new.5" = "It runs on the engine already in macOS and weighs 2.9 MB.";
